 "notes": "Direct search for scalar-field DM via BS/test-mass size oscillations in LIGO O3. Fig.3 blue \"This work\" limit (95% CL), lower boundary of the blue excluded region, read from the embedded raster (figure is a raster inside results_combined.pdf). x-axis is DM Compton frequency; converted to mass via m[eV]=h f/c^2 using the figure bottom m_phi[eV] axis directly (10 Hz -> 4e-14 eV, ~5000 Hz -> 2e-11 eV). The paper bounds mu=Lambda_i^-2, interpreted as either Lambda_gamma^-1 (panel b, d_e) or Lambda_e^-1 (panel a, d_me) with the other set to zero; the two panels are the SAME numerical curve. Reported ScalarPhoton d_e = M_Pl/(sqrt(4pi) Lambda_gamma) = Lambda_gamma^-1 * 3.442e18 GeV (M_Pl=1.22e19 GeV, kappa=sqrt(4pi)/M_Pl); the ScalarElectron d_me curve is numerically identical. Bathtub min d_e~0.24 (Lambda^-1~7e-20 GeV^-1) near m~1.7e-13 eV. rho_local=0.4 GeV/cm^3 (not rescaled). Steep left/right walls are the 10 Hz / 5000 Hz band edges.",
